WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.370
In 1923, a man in prison
wrote a short book.

2
00:00:04.420 --> 00:00:07.850
Its title was Essentials of Hindutva.

3
00:00:07.900 --> 00:00:10.420
Hindutva means Hindu-ness.

4
00:00:10.470 --> 00:00:13.660
Its author, Savarkar, was a rationalist.

5
00:00:13.710 --> 00:00:17.930
He separated Hindutva from
Hinduism as a set of beliefs.

6
00:00:17.980 --> 00:00:21.490
So what makes someone
a Hindu: belief, birth,

7
00:00:21.540 --> 00:00:23.190
or something else?

8
00:00:23.240 --> 00:00:27.420
In this mission, you'll weigh up whether
Hindutva is the only effective Hindu

9
00:00:27.470 --> 00:00:29.720
response to a secular age.

10
00:00:29.770 --> 00:00:34.130
Then you'll hear how Hindus
themselves disagree about Hindutva.

11
00:00:34.180 --> 00:00:38.730
Your mission: find out how Hindutva
decides who counts as a Hindu,

12
00:00:38.780 --> 00:00:40.990
and why Hindus disagree about it.
